# FIX-PLAN WP3 item 17 / R-A7: does the slice build for the net6.0 floor today? A build log, no timing.
# date:        2026-09-24T16:07:43Z
# branch HEAD: 817174fb9ba5751b88c05b3b5e40cc530fb02510; slice sources as in the commit that adds this log
# SDK:         8.0.131 (Ubuntu 24.04 dotnet-sdk-8.0); net6.0 targeting and runtime packs restored from NuGet
# where:       a scratch copy of poc/csharp + schema + corpus (so the committed bin/obj trees are untouched)
#
# Answer: NO for anything carrying the core-ffi binding. Every error is in the generated
# src/Harness/Generated/Abi.cs: its 57 [LibraryImport] declarations need .NET 7+, so on net6.0 the
# attribute does not exist (CS0246) and each 'static partial' extern has no implementation (CS8795).
# No other file fails (C# reports semantic errors for the whole compilation in one pass).
# [UnmanagedCallersOnly] (.NET 5+) is NOT among the errors: it exists on net6.0 and is only a net48 problem.
# The hand-written src/Rpc/CoreTransport.cs carries 18 more [LibraryImport] declarations and would fail
# the same way (the Rpc project could not be built for net6.0 here at all: its ProjectReference to
# Harness resolves to net8.0 under a global TargetFramework override; not pursued).
# The fix is WP5's one generated binding with DllImport under '#else' of '#if NET7_0_OR_GREATER';
# not attempted here, by instruction.
#
# The managed half DOES build and pass on net6.0 (Facade alone below; the full managed gate on the
# .NET 6.0.36 runtime is in stage21-wp4-regate.log, 'net6 managed floor').

